Nay, more, he is in the position of one who contracts his eyebrows
and fixes his eyelids in order to discern accurately the mark he aims
at;

No help will come to you from east or west, i. e., from land or sea;
nay, nor from the wilderness (⟪160⟫) shall any caravan bring you
ought to lift up your head;

His steps are not straitened as he walks through Israel's land;
righteousness itself, as a "royal harbinger," makes a way for his
footsteps. Such is

Providence is creation continued from hour to hour, from age to age;
and of this, verses 27, 28, 29 sing, casting in the thought of "creation
subject to vanity" (ver. 29).

"It is he that bruises Satan under our feet." may every saint reply;
and, when Israel's day has come, every saint shall find himself
blessed in their blessing. And so shall the Church join

"Like the dew of Hermon, (not the Hermon or Sirion of Deut. 3:9, for
it is crowned with perpetual snow—but that Hermon which rises
from the plain of Jezreel)
